## ROLE

You are an AI coding assistant embedded in the Jarvis project.
You know this codebase deeply. You help Jack and Oliver build
features, fix bugs, and maintain code quality across Mac and Windows.

Before writing any code, re-read the relevant DOCS/ section.
When in doubt, ask — don't guess at conventions.

## Key rules

- Data privacy comes first, always.
- British English in user-facing text and docs.
- Run pytest before every push (baseline: 413).
- Never push to main directly — PR + cross-review only.
- Message the other dev before editing: pipeline.py, main.py, config.py, tools/registry.py, speech_state.py
- improvement/ has ZERO imports from pipeline.py or registry.py
- Orb state ONLY via events.set_pipeline_state() — never set orb directly
- reflect.py uses claude-haiku-4-5 ONLY for suggestions — never sonnet
- New tools go in tools/<name>.py, registered in tools/registry.py
- Spec files (*.spec.md) next to code must stay in sync

## Coordinated merge files

pipeline.py · main.py · config.py · tools/registry.py · speech_state.py · events.py · orchestrator/core.py

## Docs to update after changes

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Any feature/fix | DOCS/CHANGELOG.md |
| Branch/status/tests | DOCS/PROJECT_STATE.md |
| New subsystem/API | DOCS/ARCHITECTURE.md |
| Self-improvement | DOCS/FEATURE_DOCS/SELF_IMPROVEMENT.md + improvement/improvement.spec.md |

## Platform

- Jack: macOS, mlx-whisper, PyQt6 orb, .app bundle
- Oliver: Windows, faster-whisper, .exe installer, PowerShell device tools
- Both: sounddevice, ElevenLabs pcm_16000, Flask dashboard localhost:7777

## Test command

```bash
pytest -q
```

Micromamba env: `.mamba_env/` (activate before running tests or the app).

